flowchart LR
  accTitle: A connection can end without ending the agent
  accDescr: The local terminal runs a client. SSH or a provider exec API connects the client to a bridge on a Linux host. Through a private Unix socket, the bridge reaches a persistent holder. The holder owns the agent's PTY, an 8 MiB output ring and a separate shadow terminal for screen snapshots. The bridge ends with the connection; the holder keeps running.

  client[Your terminal and client]

  subgraph host[Your Linux host]
    bridge[Bridge]
    subgraph session[Session: survives disconnects]
      holder[Holder]
      agent[Agent PTY]
      ring[Output ring: 8 MiB]
      shadow[Shadow VT: snapshots]
      holder <--> agent
      holder -.-> ring
      holder -.-> shadow
    end
    bridge <-->|Private Unix socket| holder
  end

  client <-->|SSH or provider exec| bridge
  classDef persistent fill:#fff7ed,stroke:#c2410c,color:#7c2d12
  class holder,agent,ring,shadow persistent
